      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Arx Mentis [zone=1022]\n**Who:**\n- Firiona Vie [npc=47747]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 105\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Related Zones:**\n- Arx Mentis: All Rivers Lead to the Sea [zone=1036]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Al`Kabor [npc=48631]\n- Atrox Lacerta [npc=48632]\n- Dabner Drednever [npc=48633]\n- Dagda Icefury [npc=48634]\n- Firiona Vie [npc=48635]\n- Galeth Veredeth [npc=48636]\n- Holmein the Hated [npc=48637]\n- Lyirae Oakwynd [npc=48638]\n- Ognit Eznertob [npc=48639]\n- The Unseen, Unheard Helper [npc=48640]\n- Thubr Axebringer [npc=48641]\n- a chest - All Rivers Lead to the Sea [npc=48691]\n- a citadel tinkerer [npc=48625]\n- a cryo operari [npc=48626]\n- a medicus praetor [npc=48338]\n- a plated construct [npc=48628]\n- a sicarius praetor [npc=48629]\n- a vindex praetor [npc=48630]\n**Related Quests:**\n- TDS Progression #0: An Overview [quest=7701]\n- TDS Progression #21: A Beginning From an End [quest=7723]\n- TDS Progression #23: The Cost of Balance [quest=7725]\n**Era:** | !The Darkened Sea\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sun Oct 26 03:00:18 2014\nModified: Sat Feb 21 23:43:58 2026 |\n---\n\n**The Darkened Sea Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This group mission begins with Firiona Vie ( **click for map image**) in Arx Mentis, located at the zone-in._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Completion of \"A Rising Storm\" (Tempest Temple)\n\\- Completion of \"Gathering Clouds\" (Tempest Temple)\n\\- Completion of \"Clearer Skies\" (Tempest Temple)\n\\- Completion of \"The Edge of Balance\" (Katta Castrum: Deluge)\n\\- Completion of \"The Abscent Scholar\" (Katta Castrum: Deluge)\n\\- Completion of \"Just Recompense\" (Brother Island)\n\\- Completion of \"The Cover of Night\" (Brother Island)\n\\- Completion of \"Loyal is the Heart\" (Caverns of Endless Song)\n\\- Completion of \"Leave No Brother Behind\" (Caverns of Endless Song)\n\\- Completion of \"Two Sides of the Shield\" (Caverns of Endless Song)\n\\- Completion of \"The Sacred Profaned\" (Degmar, the Lost Castle)\n\\- Completion of \"Crying for the Dead\" (Degmar, the Lost Castle)\n\\- Completion of \"Burden of the Past\" (Degmar, the Lost Castle)\n\\- Completion of \"An Endless Cycle\" (Thuliasaur Island)\n\\- Completion of \"To Remake Eden\" (Thuliasaur Island)\n\\- Completion of \"Fit for the New World\" (Thuliasaur Island)\n\\- Completion of \"A Fickle Wind Blows\" (Combine Dredge)\n\\- Completion of \"What Hate Begets\" (Combine Dredge)\n\\- Completion of \"Deep Lies the Snow\" (Combine Dredge)\n\\- Completion of \"Free Us From Ourselves\" (Arx Mentis)\n\\- Completion of \"A Beginning From an End\" (Arx Mentis)\n_Say \"rescue\" to request the task and \"go\" to zone in._\nYou say, 'Hail, Firiona Vie'\nFiriona Vie looks up at the citadel. 'Our [path] lies above us. We will rescue our friends who were taken from the [ship]. We shall not be defeated by [Lanys]!'\nYou say, 'Lanys?'\nFiriona Vie cannot quite stop her hands from shaking. 'She would do to them what was done to us by Discord -- and worse. I was not broken by my captivity, but Lanys would break me with the captivity of my friends... it shall not [happen]'\nYou say, 'What will happen?'\nFiriona Vie says 'We shall [storm] the citadel and rescue them. We have their locations. We must not [wait].'\nYou say, 'Why not wait?'\nFiriona Vie says 'Lanys sends us onto the ice, assuring us it can bear our weight. I see the frigid waters beneath us, but every minute we debate brings my friends closer to the cold of death.'\nYou say, 'How should we storm it?'\nFiriona Vie says 'We shall be the thunderheads that gather above Lanys. Our cold shall bury her in snows that pile up to the stars. First we shall [rescue] our friends. Then the storm shall begin.'\nYou say, 'All right, we'll rescue them...'\nFiriona Vie says 'Then we shall [go].'\nYou have been assigned the task 'All Rivers Lead to the Sea'.\nLanys and Calix are holding Firiona's friends in the citadel, torturing and experimenting upon them. Firiona is leading the charge to save them from their fates.\n\n---\n\n!\n\n---\n\n_This is a fairly straightforward task. Hail, follow the Quest NPCs, kill mobs to rescue an NPC, repeat until finished._\nSpeak with Firiona 0/1 (Arx Mentis)\nYou say, 'Hail, Firiona Vie'\nFiriona Vie says, 'We divide here. Find the rooms on the map. I do not know what awaits us... Prepare yourselves. Adventurers, you are with me.'\n\n---\n\nMeet Firiona in the Clockwork Construction Room to look for Galeth 0/1 (Arx Mentis)\nOgnit Eznertob looks around at the scattered pieces of clockworks and other constructs. 'They have already broken him... Galeth's pieces must be in here somewhere...'\n\n---\n\nKill the tinkerers and constructs to find out what happened to Galeth 0/9 (Arx Mentis)\n_These mobs are splittable from each other and mezzable. They each hit for a max ~22,000. The plated constructs in particular have a lot of hitpoints._\nSpeak with Ognit about the pieces of Galeth's body 0/3 (Arx Mentis)\nOgnit Eznertob says 'He's badly damaged, but I'll do as much as I can.'\nOgnit Eznertob says 'If only I had more skill...'\nFiriona Vie says 'Father!'\nSpeak with Galeth 0/9 (Arx Mentis)\nGaleth Veredeth twists his limbs around and flexes his fingers. 'Still stiff, but what can a man with metal joints who has just been vivisected expect? I sail on, though my fingers may not close around the oar.'\nOgnit Eznertob says, 'This is the best I can do with the time we have. It is quick and unstable. Please, Galeth, keep yourself together until I can do it properly...'\nFiriona Vie looks at the cracks and gouges in Galeth's body. 'Father... what did they do to you? What did they do to our friends?'\nGaleth Veredeth's eyes shine with their unchanging light. 'There is nothing they can do to me. I am beyond physical pain. The only pain I felt was that of seeing pain inflicted on our companions' flesh as Lanys' minions beat them and gave them over to the researchers. That was the last I saw of them, but still the pain lingers -- a feeling I have not recalled for a long time...'\nFiriona Vie looks away. 'I am sorry I brought you from your home, back to a world of pain...'\nGaleth Veredeth continues to look at his daughter. 'I never wished to feel such things again. The emotions had faded slowly over the years, and I was at rest. But Tunare has called us, and her will must be done. Only then may we return to her and rest in her peace.'\nOgnit Eznertob looks at the ground. 'If only I were better at magic and tinkering, none of this would have happened. Things would be different.'\nFiriona Vie says, 'If only so many things had happened differently... If only I had killed Lanys in Kithicor... If only we had both remained in our prisons for eternity. But the snows fall and feed the rivers that run into the sea...'\nFiriona Vie says, 'We keep moving. We have no other choice. We find Thubr. Come.'\n\n---\n\nFind Thubr in the Teleporter Room 0/1 (Arx Mentis)\nAs you near the teleporter room, a guttural roar rips through the hallways, accompanied by the clash of steel.\nKill the guards attacking Thubr 0/3 (Arx Mentis)\n_These three mobs are aggro-linked and immune to all forms of crowd control. They each hit less than standard mobs for the zone (about a max ~10,000), but have a lot of hitpoints._\nSpeak with Thubr 0/9 (Arx Mentis)\nThubr Axebringer is covered in blood. He shakes with rage and shock as you approach him. He almost swings the sword at your head before recognizing you. 'I killed 'em, each one of 'em, and I'll kill the rest! And this time they've all earned it...'\nThubr Axebringer's eyes are clear. He is breathing hard. 'It's nearly gone... the sin, the mistake, the flesh that brought me misery on that night...' Thubr holds up his right arm. His hand is maimed and covered in blood.\nFiriona Vie reaches out. 'Thubr, your hand...'\nThubr Axebringer looks at the jagged flesh. 'Sorry, Firiona, I won't be much use to ya now...'\nFiriona Vie begins binding Thubr's wound. 'Do not say that... You are alive, and that is all I ask of you.'\nFiriona Vie finishes binding Thubr's wound and staunching the bleeding. 'Where do these portals lead?'\nThubr Axebringer lowers the sword and holds his injured arm. 'I stepped on 'em while fighting, but nothing happened.'\nOgnit Eznertob says, 'They must be controlled by a keying system.'\nGaleth Veredeth says, 'Leave them be. Let us find Lyirae.'\n\n---\n\nFind Lyirae at the Feeding Chambers 0/1 (Arx Mentis)\nYou hear a shout from the corner of the corridor, and you find Lyirae struggling to defend herself against a massive lizard.\nKill the Atrox Lacerta 0/1 (Arx Mentis)\n_This mob is leashed to its spawn point and sees through invisibility. It hits for a max ~23,000; summons from 100% health; single-target rampages; and casts the 35' range PBAE \"Flesh Rip\" (57,000 unmitigated damage). If pulled from its spawn point, it warps back, drops all aggro, and strips its debuffs._\nSpeak with Lyirae 0/9 (Arx Mentis)\nLyirae Oakwynd bows her head. 'You came for me... You risked your lives. You should not have...'\nLyirae Oakwynd continues. 'It is fate that robs me of my friends... Do not let it be my own safety that does so...'\nGaleth Veredeth says, 'You are a drop in the stream, Lyirae, as are we all. You cannot climb upon its banks and watch us all pass\nLyirae Oakwynd looks up. 'Galeth, you are whole! Thubr... your hand!'\nThubr Axebringer grunts, 'Lost in the stream, as Galeth might say.'\nLyirae Oakwynd says, 'Where are Dagda and Dabner? Dagda was still unconscious when they dragged us into the citadel and the guards started beating us...'\nFiriona Vie says, 'We'll find them -- our friends and those responsible for their suffering. Lyirae, did you see Al`Kabor pass by here?'\nLyirae Oakwynd says, 'No... Why would he pass by if you sent him to help?'\nFiriona Vie scowls. 'We must find him. He has already run off once before on this journey, and the consequences were dire. I cannot have this happen again.'\n\n---\n\nFind and speak with Al'Kabor 0/6 (Arx Mentis)\nAl`Kabor nods. 'Such an unparalleled accomplishment in the magical arts -- this citadel is the apex of learning. To destroy it or ignore all that it could teach would be a shame.'\nFiriona Vie's eyes are stern. 'This is not the time. Dagda and Dabner are in danger. I do not care about what you want. Your whims and intellectual curiosities threaten us all! Have you learned nothing?!'\nAl`Kabor raises an eyebrow. 'Firiona, what I learn here might save everyone. You must learn to recognize your enemies. I shall remain here and study the citadel. I trust you have enough bodies and righteous anger to save Dagda and Dabner.'\nOgnit Eznertob slams his staff on the floor. 'I can't believe I ever trusted you as my teacher! You... you only think of yourself! How could you put a few books and scraps of knowledge above the lives of your friends?! I'm done trying to emulate someone like you!'\nAl`Kabor says calmly. 'That is smart. You were not good at it.'\nFiriona Vie looks coolly at Al`Kabor. 'You have caused nothing but trouble this entire journey. You can stay here and do what you wish. Those who actually care shall save Dagda and Dabner.'\n\n---\n\nFind the Cyro Chamber 0/1 (Arx Mentis)\n_Once you enter the basement, you won't be able to exit it._\nKill the cyro operari 0/8 (Arx Mentis)\n_These mobs have low aggro and assist ranges (you can pull each of them single, except for a pair in the back of the room). Each hits for a max ~20,000; is mezzable; and casts \"Thick Ice\" (single-target stun + nuke for 40,000 dmg)._\nSpeak with Dabner 0/9 (Arx Mentis)\nDabner Drednever is shivering. The blood trail beneath his nose has frozen. 'Firiona... is it you?' Dabner struggles to sit up. 'Where is Dagda?'\nDabner Drednever yells, 'Dagda!' Her skin already turning blue, Dagda lies next to Dabner, her wounded leg frozen. 'Do something! She's still breathing!'\nOgnit Eznertob hastily casts a spell of warmth. The ice begins to melt, and Dagda's wounds start to bleed afresh.\nDabner Drednever begins casting the most powerful healing spells he can remember, but Dagda's wounds remain.\nDagda Icefury groans, and her eyes open halfway. Her voice is a whisper. 'Dabner, you're safe... we're all safe... safe in the warmth... just let it embrace you. Don't fear it.'\nDabner Drednever's voice quavers. 'Yes, you're safe now. Firiona is here; I'm here. We're going to get you out, back to the Swift Fin.'\nFiriona Vie looks away from Dagda. 'Back to Halas, back to your home. Back to fishing, drinking, and fighting. Back to a time before I brought you to this dark place...'\nDagda Icefury clothes begin to darken with blood. Her companions can now see the cuts and slashes under her clothes, the patches of skin pierced with metal. She tries to laugh but can only sigh. 'We cannot go back... I was already too old, and now... too broken. The snow lies too deeply upon me...'\nDabner Drednever wipes away a tear and tries uselessly to stop the bleeding. 'It's not too late! We can still...'\nSpeak with Dabner again 0/13 (Arx Mentis)\nOgnit Eznertob kneels on the other side of Dagda and tries applying pressure to her wounds. Lyirae and Firiona tend to Dagda's leg, but the dying flesh is cold to the touch.\nDabner Drednever is silent. His eyes do not leave Dagda's face. 'Dagda, you know I love you. I always have. I... can't let you die without hearing it from my lips...'\nDagda Icefury's eyes open all the way. They are bright, like a river in sunlight. 'I know... You are my brother, Dabner... and you, Ognit...' She clasps their hands. 'You know I loved you both... as family... I was your shield, and you my light...'\nDabner Drednever's tears begin falling. 'I'm sorry... I ran from you... I couldn't do more... I couldn't...'\nOgnit Eznertob shouts 'Apply more pressure! Cast another spell!'\nFiriona Vie shouts 'Keep talking to us, Dagda!'\nLyirae Oakwynd shouts 'Dagda, don't close your eyes! Don't!'\nThubr Axebringer shouts 'Strength! You were always the best fighter of us two!'\nGaleth Veredeth says calmly, 'Dagda, the river flows, and you are a part of it. It carries you. Feel its warmth. It carries you to the sea, where we will all meet you again someday, my friend.'\nDagda Icefury's eyes struggle open. 'I... always wanted to die with a sword in my hand. But... now I have found something better... to die with my family's hands in mine...' Dagda closes her eyes.\nDabner Drednever's tears stream down his face. 'Dagda! Dagda...' He and Ognit continue holding Dagda's hands, even after her hands no longer hold theirs.\nLyirae Oakwynd shakes her head. Another lost beneath the waves...\nFiriona Vie stands up. She cannot keep her vision from blurring. 'Yes, friend, someday together again in that vast sea...'\n\n---\n\nSpeak with the Unseen, Unheard Helper 0/5 (Arx Mentis)\n**TASK LOCKS HERE**\n_Be ready for a fight._\nYou read out loud the note the helper hands to you. 'Firiona, how do you feel at this moment? Have you received my gift? Do you feel the hatred? Perhaps you will when all your friends are dead -- and your family, and your people, and your god...'\nYou continue reading. 'You are nothing without hate. Our lives have been guided by it, shaped by it. You despise it, but it has made you. Now you shall embrace it.'\nYou continue reading. 'You see this man before you, unseen and unheard? He is the hatred that knocks at your heart. He is the figure that creeps up to your windows at night and raps on the panes, searching for a way inside.'\nYou continue reading. 'He selected the blades and the metals, made the incisions in Dagda's flesh, loosed the poisons into her body, and made her a gift for you. He can no longer speak or see, but since when does hatred rely upon the senses?'\nYou continue reading. 'Now I give him to you: another gift for my twin!'\n_Holmein the Hated appears at its location and immediately aggro's._\nKill Holmein the Hated 0/1 (Arx Mentis)\nHolmein the Hated has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nHolmein the Hated twitches as his blood pools around him. Before he dies he dips his finger in the blood and writes, 'Citadel Apex.'\n_Holmein the Hated hits for a max ~24,000 and AE rampages. Every 25 seconds, he casts the spell \"Tainted Blood\" on a random target (targeted 15' range AE for 75,000 dmg + DOT for 8,333/tick). Every 25 seconds, he casts \"Open Wound\" on a random target (nuke for 61,000 dmg + debuff that increase \"Tainted Blood\" nuke to 105,000 dmg)._\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Firiona 0/9 (Arx Mentis)\n_Hail her until the task completes._\nFiriona Vie watches Holmein until his body stops twitching and his chest stops rising. She turns to Dagda and feels the tears start to form again. Dabner is weeping. 'Lanys will die for this, just as Holmein has.'\nGaleth Veredeth looks at Firiona with his unchanging eyes. 'Do not forget that you are the Champion of Balance.'\nFiriona Vie's eyes are hard. 'I will not forget anything.'\nDabner Drednever's tears fall. 'We must take her back to the Swift Fin, back to Halas... We can't leave her in this place... Need to give her a funeral... a nice one, like you had, Firiona...'\nFiriona Vie looks around at her companions: Dabner crying inconsolably, Lyirae staring into the distance, Thubr's wound beginning to bleed again. 'Thubr and Lyirae, take Dabner and Dagda back through the portal, to the ship. Sail back to Brother Island, away from here. That's an order!'\nOgnit Eznertob says, 'Firiona?'\nFiriona Vie looks at Ognit. 'You can still fight?'\nOgnit Eznertob nods. 'Yes.'\nFiriona Vie says, 'Good. You and Galeth are coming with me. We are bringing down the citadel -- and Lanys with it. Let us [leave].'\n_A chest with loot also spawns at this time. The task is repeatable with a 6-hour lockout timer from the time of request._\n_Rewards:_\n112 platinum, 5 gold\nExperience\n_Possible Chest Loot (1 item + 0-1 armor templates + 0-1 Briny Essence 0-1 Valiant ornament):_\nArx Medallion\nBuffer of the Quastori\nCore of Caldarius\nRomance's Runic Rampart\nSparking Bauble\nHighwater Armguards\nHighwater Boots\nHighwater Bracer\nHighwater Gloves\nHighwater Helm\nHighwater Leggings\nHighwater Tunic\nMedian Briny Essence\nGreater Briny Essence\nGlowing Briny Essence",
